  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>I am finally itching to start actually coding again. Most of my coding time has been spent just taking notes and trying to learn as much as possible about <fr:link href="/5PSC/" title="Kernel DSLs" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5PSC/" display-uri="5PSC" type="local">kernel DSLs</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link>, etc. However, I need to exercise some coding chops.</html:p>
    <html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmicy3ffywtqloo5j3zdjvzsukc6uglftxqjf6z6mgspjvntzyij4uq.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Coding hours for week 2026-W32.</html:figcaption></html:figure>
    <html:p>There is no non-coding computer time because arbtt is a very lightweight program with no synchronization across devices. Qualitatively, I am jumping around too much again. I do not know if arbtt can properly capture this, but I need to be more disciplined with the pomodoro method. Specifically, choosing something to work on and not diverging <html:strong>for anything</html:strong> until the timer has ended.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
